  "body": "From the merge-order analysis of 2026-11-22 (61 open PRs). `git merge-tree` and `cargo xtask merge-plan` find text conflicts only. Two PRs merged with no text conflict and were red on the merged tree today:\n\n- #2951: `agie_native.rs` did not compile, because #3232 added the field `sharp_corners` to `WireContourOp`.\n- #2921: 4 `camcraft-ui` tests failed, because a new tooltip gave a second AccessKit node the label of an existing control.\n\nMain was red two times on 2026-11-22 for the same class (#3384 after #3307 and #3108).\n\n## Necessary work\n1. Add a step to `cargo xtask merge-plan` (or a new `cargo xtask merge-trial`): make a temporary trial tree with all PRs of wave 1 merged (an octopus merge or a chain of merges), in a worktree that the tool removes again.\n2. On that tree, run `cargo check --tests` for the crates that the PRs touch. Report each error with the PR that owns the file.\n3. The `merge-ready` skill runs this step before the first merge of a wave. A PR with an error leaves the wave.\n4. Keep the disk rule: a check build only, no test binaries.\n\n## Done means\n- The tool finds the #2951 class (a missing struct field) on a recorded pair of branches in a test.\n- The `merge-ready` skill names the step. The PR has `Process change: yes`.\n",
